===== revert to Original Firmware with Win7 =====

1. Connect PC and Router with Lan

2. Set password in http://192.168.1.1

3. Disconnect Wlan

4. Set Lan IPv4  
                 IP          192.168.1.2
                 mask        255.255.255.0
                 gateway     192.168.1.1
                 DNS Server  192.168.1.1
5. start SSH Session with [[http://the.earth.li/~sgtatham/putty/latest/x86/putty.zip|Putty]]
   login root and password like 1.
6.  erase firmware partition (be patient, it's a long process):
    # mtd -r erase firmware   
7.  after the router reboots, you will see that the power led is blinking.

8. Download Firmware .zip File from [[https://www.netgear.com/support/product/WNDR4000#download|Netgear]] (tested with WNDR4000-V1.0.0.90_9.1.79.chk)

9. start [[http://www.shadowsoftware.net/shadowgameworld/downloads/tftp2.exe|TFTP2]]
   Server 192.168.1.1
   password like 1.
   File WNDR4000-V1.0.0.90_9.1.79.chk 
10. click Upgrade and wait until the Router restart

